@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
' '   description:  A simple e-commerce checkout flow with one decision point.
'   usecase:      Teach action nodes, initial/final, decision/merge, control flow.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       e-commerce
' ============================================================================
title Example Activity - Simple Checkout Flow

' The INITIAL NODE (filled circle) is written as |start|.
' It is the single entry point of an activity diagram.
start

' ACTION NODES are written as ":Label;" and render as ROUNDED RECTANGLES.
' The trailing semicolon terminates the action label.
:Browse product catalog;

:Add item to shopping cart;

:Enter shipping details;

' A DECISION NODE tests a condition and splits the flow into outgoing branches.
'   Syntax: if (cond) then (label-yes) ... else (label-no) ... endif
' The parenthesized labels annotate the edges leaving the decision.
if (Payment valid?) then (yes)
  :Process payment;
else (no)
  :Show payment error;
  :Offer alternate payment method;
endif

' Both branches converge here. This rejoin point is the implicit MERGE NODE.
' A merge simply reunites alternative flows — no synchronization occurs.
:Confirm outcome to customer;

' The FINAL NODE (bullseye) is written as |stop| and ends the activity.
stop

' TEACHING NOTES:
'   - An arrow between two nodes is a CONTROL FLOW edge.
'   - There is exactly one initial node; there may be many final nodes.
'   - Decision and merge often come as a pair (split then rejoin).
@enduml
